@startuml alert-scope-filtering-flow
title GET /alerts Server-Side Scope Filtering (CP2)

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #CCCCCC
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA

actor "Operator or\nDemo viewer" as Op
participant "Dashboard" as UI #E0E7FF
participant "API\n(requireAuth)" as API #DBEAFE
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts" as DB #FEF9C3

Op -> UI : opens alerts widget
UI -> API : GET /alerts[?bbox=...]
API -> DB : SELECT ... WHERE status IN ('NEW','ACKNOWLEDGED')

alt role == operator
  API -> API : load saved user_workspaces scope
  alt no saved workspace
    API --> UI : 200 [] (empty -- show scope setup prompt)
  else scope exists
    API -> API : matchesScope(row, {bounds, entity_types, alert_types})\nfor every fetched row
    API --> UI : 200 [...only in-scope rows...]
  end
else role == demo
  alt bbox provided
    API -> API : matchesScope(row, {bounds: bbox, entity_types: null, alert_types: null})\nfor every fetched row
    API --> UI : 200 [...rows within bbox only...]
  else no bbox
    API --> UI : 200 [...every fetched row, unfiltered...]
    note right of API
      Transitional: nothing sends bbox yet
      (dashboard alert widget doesn't pass
      the map viewport until CP5's frontend
      work wires it up). Safe fallback --
      matches today's existing behavior.
    end note
  end
end

note over API, DB
  Position always read from the alert's own payload
  (immutable at detection time), never current Redis
  state. Field path differs by alert_type -- see
  ADR-012. A row whose type yields no known position
  (only possible for ROUTE_DEVIATION today) is excluded,
  never included by a fallback guess.
end note

@enduml
